    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// The lookup node above replaces our data with whatever row it found (or\n// {} via Always Output Data if nothing matched, or an {error: ...} shaped\n// item if the sheet is missing a filtered-on column) -- recover the real\n// message data (and its binary attachments) from before the lookup, and\n// just carry forward whether a real row was found.\n//\n// 'row_number' is NOT the found-signal here (this sheet may not even have\n// that column). Use the Sheets node's own always-attached 'row_number'\n// metadata field instead -- present on every real matched row regardless\n// of which actual columns that row has. Matching is done on timestamp +\n// fromEmail + toEmail + subject (see the lookup node) since those columns\n// exist on every row ever logged, old and new, by either provider.\nconst lookupResult = $input.first().json;\nconst original = $('Extract Tab Name').item;\nreturn [{\n  json: { ...original.json, _alreadyLogged: !!(lookupResult && lookupResult.row_number !== undefined) },\n  binary: original.binary\n}];"
      },
