    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Get previous node data -- drop tabName, it's routing metadata (which\n// tab of the conversation sheet to write to) used by upstream/downstream\n// nodes, not a column that belongs in the sheet itself.\nconst { tabName, ...previousData } = $('Message Already Logged?').item.json;\n\n// When a message has no attachments, 'If Has Attachments'' false branch\n// feeds this node the single ORIGINAL message item untouched -- NOT a\n// Drive file result. That item's own `id` is the Outlook message id\n// (e.g. 'AAMkADEzYjVk...'), so treating it as a fallback Drive file id\n// synthesized a bogus drive.google.com link on every attachment-less row.\n// Only ever read $input as Drive results when this message actually went\n// through the attachment branch.\n//\n// 'Drive | Upload Attachment' has no explicit `fields` option, so its\n// response isn't guaranteed to include webViewLink -- only `id` is\n// guaranteed on any real Drive file response. Rebuild the same canonical\n// URL Drive itself uses (confirmed identical to what the search path\n// already returns) from the id whenever webViewLink itself didn't come\n// back, instead of silently saving a blank link for a file that really is\n// sitting in Drive.\nconst links = previousData.hasAttachments\n  ? $input.all()\n      .map(item => item.json.webViewLink\n        || (item.json.id ? `https://drive.google.com/file/d/${item.json.id}/view?usp=drivesdk` : null))\n      .filter(link => !!link)\n  : [];\n\n// Collect all webViewLinks -- named 'webViewLink1'/'webViewLink2'/... to\n// match the conversation sheet's actual existing header columns. A prior\n// version of this named them 'attachment1'/'attachment2', which didn't\n// match any existing header, so autoMapInputData created a brand new\n// 'attachment1' column instead of populating the real webViewLink1/2\n// columns every other row (Gmail included) already uses.\nconst linkFields = {};\nlinks.forEach((link, index) => {\n  linkFields[`webViewLink${index + 1}`] = link;\n});\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      ...previousData,\n      ...linkFields\n    }\n  }\n];\n"
      },
